      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Sure, here are multiple test cases with as many bullet points as possible to meet your coverage requirements for the SentinelGate Firewall Layer:\n\n1. Functional Verification:\n   - Ensure SentinelGate inspects and drops packets from blocked CIDR ranges.\n   - Check for proper packet inspection at Layer 7 for SQL injection strings.\n   - Confirm that SentinelGate does not allow expired SSL certificates to pass.\n   - Verify that SentinelGate can handle both single and simultaneous IP block verifications.\n   - Test SentinelGate handling of UDP packets, as UDP does not inherently have fragmented packets like TCP.\n   - Inspect SentinelGate behavior with fragmented TCP packets, including different TCP fragment offsets.\n   - Confirm SentinelGate can inspect IPv6 packets, as IPv6 has a different structure compared to IPv4.\n   - Ensure SentinelGate can handle packets with malformed IP headers.\n   - Verify that SentinelGate correctly drops packets with invalid TCP flag combinations.\n   - Monitor SentinelGate's response to packets with unexpected ICMP types/commands.\n   - Test SentinelGate behavior when encountering packets with malformed DNS headers.\n   - Ensure SentinelGate can handle high-density traffic scenarios without packet loss or delay.\n   - Investigate SentinelGate's handling of TCP window size and Adjust Window acknowledgment.",
